  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the infantilizing self-introduction scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the scene where the man with Down syndrome is depicted with the text overlay 'the name's bob... bob', which infantilizes him and reduces his identity to a simplistic, repetitive self-introduction. This creates a semiotic projection where the viewer is implicitly invited to see themselves in the role of the person being infantilized or to perceive the scene as a humorous, simplistic portrayal of disability. The projection is not explicit (e.g., no 'you' or 'me' text), but the framing and the stereotype reinforce a user identification with the infantilized subject or the ableist perspective.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
